      ],
      "matched_phrases": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
          "matched_text": "Set Aside",
          "start": 151,
          "end": 160
        }
      ],
      "text_preview": "\nOther Details :\n Date Of Institution : 05.02.2018\n Date Of Reserving Order : 09.04.2024\n Date Of Order : 09.05.2024\n Appeal U/S. 374 (3) Cr. P. C. To Set Aside The\n Impugned Judgment Dated 16.12.2017 & Order\nOn Sentence Dated 06.01.2018, P"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "786cd41135ee4f869df1fde8803d8b81_3",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "1. The appellant is aggrieved by the impugned judgment dated 16/12/2017 of Ld. MM-02,\nSouth-East District, Saket Courts, vide which he was convicted for offence U/s. 279/304A IPC and by order on sentence dated 06/01/2018 vide which he was s"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3f78fa3b10e14b3d88a52490d2b37614_4",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "He was sentenced to undergo Simple Imprisonment of six months for offence U/s. 279 IPC, in case FIR No.\n778/2007, PS Okhla Industrial Area, U/s. 279/304A IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "66cbf1b5958e48b987b975c39a4766c8_5",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Both the sentences were directed to run concurrently."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0c4b224f23734448b8744552e21dff47_33",
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "labels": [
        "RLC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_labels:RLC"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "5. Upon hearing the final arguments from both sides, Ld. Trial Court vide its judgment dated 16/12/2017 held the appellant/accused guilty of offence U/s. 279/304A IPC and sentenced him vide order on sentence dated 06/01/2018."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2e59c66296db464085321f89d9025b3c_62",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Hon'ble Supreme Court has held in Ravi Kapur Vs. State of Rajasthan (2012) 9 SCC 284 that -\n12.Rash and negligent driving has to be examined in the light of facts and circumstances of a given case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "274905cd485a48f485d3a180208002ee_63",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is a fact incapable of being construed or seen in isolation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7d93d9e0ad1e4eb6a4526cbf4bf3ee78_64",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It must be examined in the light of attended circumstances."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "459c233a67d74d6db6171eef76361ffa_65",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "A person who drives a vehicle on the road is liable to be held responsible for the act as well as for the result."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6a3309dac3c448668e569c5bb8665f23_66",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It may not be always possible to determine with reference to the speed of a vehicle whether a person was driving rashly and negligently."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "229281b29b2548479a3341fe9b56c60b_67",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Both these acts presuppose an abnormal conduct."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "57199f8498fb4e07870edf9f04b53930_68",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Even when one is driving a vehicle at a slow speed but recklessly and negligently, it would amount to \"rash and negligent driving\" within the meaning of language of Section 279 IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9c7a6cb5a9d7463c80958f51d3314563_69",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "That is why the Legislature in its wisdom has used the words \"manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "15fcee615bed4a3ba52f96a5f8ac1ac9_70",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The preliminary condition, thus, are that - (a) it is the manner in which the vehicle is driven; (b) it be driven either rashly or negligently; and (c) such rash or negligent driving should be such as to endanger human life."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "36a419042bb6420dacffebb399264004_71",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Once these ingredients are satisfied, the penalty contemplated under Section 279 IPC is attracted."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "36c1dfed58bd4991ae4f824da0953757_72",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n13.'Negligence' means omission to do something which a reasonable and prudent person guided by the considerations which ordinary regulate human affairs would do or doing something which a prudent and reasonable person guided by similar con"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5fa75df1855145c6b8d321dc7bbcc443_73",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Negligence is not an absolute term but is a relative one; it is rather a comparative term."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9caca38d3d2547509ae5e2883ddb76d8_74",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is difficult to state with precision any mathematically exact formula by which negligence or lack of it can be infallibly measured in a given case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e6bb7a8ff35143198b022bb1190597ba_75",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Whether there exists negligence per se or the course of conduct amounts to negligence will normally depend upon the attending and surrounding facts and circumstances which have to be taken into consideration by the Court."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2e6ae9d41c3e41f283eb7e3ac2b76642_76",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In a given case, even not doing what one was ought to do can constitute negligence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f0570fda25d04bcda67e98362dd82986_77",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n14.The Court has to adopt another parameter i.e. 'reasonable care' in determining the question of negligence or contributory negligence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "980d4f2752014c0c88677d9fa4fb070d_78",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The doctrine of reasonable care imposes an obligation or a duty upon a person (for example a driver) to care for the pedestrian on the road and this duty attains a higher degree when the pedestrians happen to be children of tender years."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "06971a1a15a0415d80148b8321e4b714_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is axiomatic to say that while driving a vehicle on a public way, there is an implicit duty cast on the drivers to see that their driving does not endanger the life of the right users of the road, may be either vehicular users or pedestr"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5bc232bd3c3f46368539e672af449ffb_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "They are expected to take sufficient care to avoid danger to others."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "93cae2ac2a7a4772ae5db9c69a7b1bb0_81",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "15.The other principle that is pressed in aid by the courts in such cases is the doctrine of res ipsa loquitur."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e54c4f67a7a64392be4bbfc7427dfd21_82",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This doctrine serves two purposes - one that an accident may by its nature be more consistent with its being caused by negligence for which the opposite party is responsible than by any other causes and that in such a case, the mere fact of"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8db13e1d462c43669be670b8da9d1b11_83",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Secondly, it is to avoid hardship in cases where the claimant is able to prove the accident but cannot prove how the accident occurred."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2094ca539b2046dc887358fc89c69db2_84",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The courts have also applied the principle of res ipsa loquitur in cases where no direct evidence was brought on record."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "556b846477fa4e74aaa014426dfbd9d3_85",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Act itself contains a provision which concerns with the consequences of driving vehicle dangerously alike the provision in the IPC that the vehicle is driven in a manner dangerous to public life."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4dd9bc239230416d918d23d11265d37e_86",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Where a person does such an offence he is punished as per the provisions of Section 184 of the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1bbafe1920ee4010842827c9dafa00a3_87",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The courts have also taken the concept Rajbir vs The State on 9 May, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/135484284/\n5 of 'culpable rashness' and 'culpable negligence' into consideration in cases of road accidents."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5534a56820364145bf6b9f3f6f39580c_88",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "'Culpable rashness' is acting with the consciousness that mischievous and illegal consequences may follow but with the hope that they will not and often with the belief that the actor has taken sufficient precautions to prevent their happen"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5b2f91a9a8c6406fbf5220d0a18fccca_89",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The imputability arises from acting despite consciousness (luxuria)."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7f1a979af2354e6fbcde25ffef4cf6cb_90",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "'Culpable negligence' is acting without the consciousness that the illegal and mischievous effect will follow, but in circumstances which show that the actor has not exercised the caution incumbent upon him and that if he had, he would have"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "96c98846e2c945b4bc523586d618c817_91",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The imputability arises from the neglect of civic duty of circumspection."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "35aa5da969c74beabaf4f8b5dbefac64_92",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In such a case the mere fact of accident is prima facie evidence of such negligence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "95d473897c6e46959bd0f87625bbc9ea_93",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This maxim suggests that on the circumstances of a given case the res speaks and is eloquent because the facts stand unexplained, with the result that the natural and reasonable inference from the facts, not a conjectural inference, shows t"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8212e0e68eb942f896bf59002e20f130_95",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "13. The accident was caused during day time, at 08:00AM in month of September, on left side of the road and victim child was crushed under front left wheel of the truck driven by the accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "824bcc91889244e78fd9740287b349b0_96",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe accident could not have happened except by rash or negligent driving of the accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "beac63dac19b45d5b1324d74bdd0430b_97",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "PW1 deposed that appellant was driving his truck in a zigzag manner and at a fast speed, and, there is no reason to disbelieve his version."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9c66f16b271e41559fcce3738335fdc8_98",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Although, IO did not record statement of any other public witness,\nwho apprehended appellant at the spot, the deposition of PW1 is detailed, lucid and consistent; it withstood the test of cross-examination and is corroborated by other evide"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "296b544bba9343c5ac529dfd4fadc71f_99",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Ld. Trial Court rightly relied upon the testimony of PW1 Ajay Kumar Rai to convict the appellant."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "561d29933f58436cb0aef389c3b4fde5_100",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The appellant led no evidence in defence and gave an untenable and vacuous reply in statement U/s. 313 CrPC that his truck was stationed and he was sleeping on its roof."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "00a9a6ac015c475c81de83c94e3b33ea_101",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Another vehicle had hit the deceased and fled from the spot, whereas, he was falsely implicated in present case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f2be4f604a484dfb9e24172536ad58fb_102",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "14. In conclusion, it is observed that the impugned judgment dated 16/12/2017 is well reasoned and is based on correct appreciation of facts and evidence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "575e37aef3754424ab1ef46ed53e2349_103",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The appellant was rightly convicted for offence U/s. 279/304A IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fbfebae3dd114f2cbe26a8883fa3803e_104",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "There is no substance in appeal and, so far as it impugns the judgment of conviction, it stands dismissed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "53652f7500a44d0a8857bc10ced8404a_105",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The issue of sentence shall be considered on completion of due procedure."
    }
  ],
